.TH CLAUDE\-DESKTOP\-UPDATE 1 "2026-08-29" "claude-desktop-builder 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude\-desktop\-update \- rebuild and install Claude Desktop when upstream ships a new build
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude\-desktop\-update
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Claude Desktop is proprietary, so no repository can ship it. This command
builds it locally instead.
.PP
It asks Anthropic's download endpoint which Linux build is current, reading
only the redirect target. If that build is already installed, it prints a
line and exits without downloading anything. If a newer build has shipped, it
runs
.B /usr/libexec/claude\-desktop\-builder/build\-official.sh
to fetch Anthropic's official .deb, repackage the payload as an RPM, and
install that RPM with dnf. The built package carries an Obsoletes tag, so an
older locally built package is replaced in place.
.PP
The command must run as root. It is normally driven by
.BR claude\-desktop\-update.timer ,
which fires once a day.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Report whether a new build exists and do nothing else.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Rebuild and install even when nothing changed upstream.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short usage summary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Up to date, or the rebuild and install succeeded.
.TP
.B 2
With \-\-check only: a new upstream build is available.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/claude\-desktop\-builder/last\-build
The upstream filename of the build that was installed last.
.TP
.I /var/lib/claude\-desktop\-builder/out
Scratch directory for the built RPM. Removed when the run finishes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR dnf (8)
.PP
https://github.com/dewzor/claude\-desktop\-fedora
